{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-106814",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is \n\n*$Z$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of a matrix by a real number) because **addition of matrices in $Z$ is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, consider the matrices\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nin $Z.$ Then,\n\n$$\ndet(A+B)=det([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nHence, $A+B\\notin Z.$\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- The zero matrix belongs to $Z.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- Given any $A\\in Z,$ the additive inverse matrix $-A=(-1)\\cdot A$ is also in $Z$ since $det(-A)=(-1)^{2}\\cdot det(A)=1\\cdot 0=0,$ and $A+(-A)=O.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- Given any $A\\in Z,$ multiplication by a scalar $\\alpha \\in R$ is closed since $det(\\alpha A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot det(A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot 0=0.$ Hence, $\\alpha A\\in Z.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- Multiplication of matrices with real entries by a scalar is associative, in general.    $\\,✓$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-106814\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p></p><p>The correct answer is </p><p></p>\n<p></p><blockquote><p></p>\n<p></p><p><em><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"86\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44D TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is <strong>not</strong> a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of a matrix by a real number) because <strong>addition of matrices in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"87\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44D TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is not closed.</strong> </em></p>\n</blockquote><p></p>\n<p></p><p>For example, consider the matrices\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"88\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mrow space=\"4\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-s3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5B TEX-S3\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 2em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"padding-right: 0.5em; padding-bottom: 0.2em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3